{
 "_doc": "In-match shops (scripts/match/shops.gd, shop_stock.gd; the stock plan is docs/SOURCE_UTILITIES.md section 3, the places docs/MAP_REGIONS.md). Vendors stand at the spots each region of a hand-made map lists (regions[].shops: [x, z, stock theme]); a spot off the region's open ground moves to the nearest open tile within snap_tiles. Every vendor sells its theme's whole `sells` list, the same in every match: tonic and armor_kit everywhere, everything else in exactly one shop. Each theme fits its region (Frostgate armor, Cinder gloves and weapon tunings, a hazard ward perk in each hazard biome). The gems are the ones a hunter picked up this run, so spending means less to extract. Entries: a utility item id (content/utility), repair (armor back to full), armor_up (the next armor tier), backpack (the next pack tier, priced by Equal backpack_shop), gear:<gear id> (gloves, armor or boots, worn at the theme's gear_rar or the default; replaces what that slot holds), perk:<perk id> (Data.PERKS; a perk with a `ward` keeps that biome hazard off you). price_k: a theme's price multiplier (the Crown's premium stall). left = how many of one entry a vendor has (the host keeps count online). Never sold: keys, shards, the Revive Ember and anything found only in matches; the never list is what --shops-check scans for. Prices are run gems: utility items use their content price times util_k. bot (BotShop): the gems a bot keeps (reserve) when it buys belt items and repairs, and (upgrade_reserve) when it buys armor tiers, gear and perks.",
